// A scenario whose When cannot happen: the Given contradicts what the action needs to be available or enabled.
// Expected: the Given of 'Unready printer' contradicts its When: print is not available (When: print is enabled);
//           the Given of 'Pending print' contradicts 'start is enabled' (When: start is enabled).

Entity Printer {
    Actions: start, print
}

Role Operator.

Action start { Initiators: Operator }
Action print { Initiators: Operator }

// start has an 'enabled' specification, so the When needs start to be enabled; a pending print stops it while
// print is available
Action start is enabled means {
    print is not pending or is not available
}

// print has no 'enabled' specification, so it is enabled exactly when it is available
Scenario: Unready printer
Given print is not available
When print is executed
Then print is not available.

Scenario: Pending print
Given print is pending AND print is available
When start is executed
Then print is pending.
